aph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L45","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:45"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"methods","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Methods"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getcurrentresult","children":[{"type":"text","value":"getCurrentResult()"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getCurrentResult(): MutationObserverResult<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L165","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:165"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the observer's current result, derived from the observed\nmutation's state (or the default, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idle"},{"type":"text","value":" state if no mutation has been\nbuilt yet, e.g. before the first "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mutate()"},{"type":"text","value":" call or after "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reset()"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/MutationObserverResult.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MutationObserverResult"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TError"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TVariables"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOnMutateResult"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The observer's latest result."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"haslisteners","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hasListeners()"}]},{"type":"code","value":"hasListeners(): boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/subscribable.ts#L43","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/subscribable.ts:43"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" while at least one listener is registered, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" once they have all unsubscribed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" if at least one listener is registered."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"inherited-from","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inherited from"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Subscribable.hasListeners","lang":"ts"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"mutate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"mutate()"}]},{"type":"code","value":"mutate(variables: TVariables, options?: MutateOptions<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>): Promise<TData>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L217","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:217"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Builds a new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mutation"},{"type":"text","value":" in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MutationCache"},{"type":"text","value":" using the observer's\ncurrent options, detaches this observer from any previously observed\nmutation, attaches it to the new one, and executes it with the given\nvariables."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The optional per-call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSuccess"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSettled"},{"type":"text","value":") are\ninvoked once the mutation settles, in addition to any callbacks defined\non the observer's own options."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"variables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"variables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TVariables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The variables passed to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mutationFn"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"options-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/MutateOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MutateOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TError"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TVariables"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOnMutateResult"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSuccess"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSettled"},{"type":"text","value":" callbacks."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-4","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A promise that resolves with the mutation's data, or rejects with its error."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"example-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"await observer.mutate(\n  { title: 'New post' },\n  { onSuccess: (data) => console.log(data) },\n)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"reset","children":[{"type":"text","value":"reset()"}]},{"type":"code","value":"reset(): void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L188","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:188"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Detaches the observer from the mutation it is currently observing (if\nany) and resets the observed result back to its default, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idle"},{"type":"text","value":" state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This does not cancel an in-flight mutation; the mutation itself keeps\nrunning to completion and its own callbacks still fire, but this\nobserver stops reflecting its state and a subsequent "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mutate()"},{"type":"text","value":" call\nwill build a brand new mutation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-5","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"see","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#mutate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MutationObserver#mutate"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"example-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"observer.reset()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"setoptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"setOptions()"}]},{"type":"code","value":"setOptions(options: MutationObserverOptions<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>): void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L100","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:100"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Updates the observer's options."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mutationKey"},{"type":"text","value":" differs from the previous one (and both were\ndefined), the observer is reset, detaching it from the mutation it was\nobserving. Otherwise, if the currently observed mutation is still\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pending"},{"type":"text","value":", its options are updated in place as well."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"options-4","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/MutationObserverOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MutationObserverOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TError"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TVariables"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOnMutateResult"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The new mutation observer options. They are defaulted with "},{"type":"link","href":"QueryClient.md#defaultmutationoptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"QueryClient#defaultMutationOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" before being applied."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-6","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"example-4","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"observer.setOptions({\n  mutationFn: (variables: { title: string }) => addPost(variables),\n  onSuccess: (data) => console.log(data),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"subscribe","children":[{"type":"text","value":"subscribe()"}]},{"type":"code","value":"subscribe(listener: MutationObserverListener): () => void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/subscribable.ts#L28","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/subscribable.ts:28"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Registers a listener to be called on every update this object notifies about. Returns a function\nthat removes the listener again — call it to stop listening. The base class never drops a listener\non its own, though some subclasses clear all of theirs in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"destroy()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters-4","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"listener","children":[{"type":"text","value":"listener"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MutationObserverListener"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Called on each update, with whatever the subclass passes to its subscribers."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-7","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function that removes the listener."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"() => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"example-5","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const unsubscribe = subscribable.subscribe(() => {\n  // react to the update\n})\n\nunsubscribe()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"inherited-from-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inherited from"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Subscribable.subscribe","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2},{"id":"extends","text":"Extends","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tdata","text":"TData","level":3},{"id":"terror","text":"TError","level":3},{"id":"tvariables","text":"TVariables","level":3},{"id":"tonmutateresult","text":"TOnMutateResult","level":3},{"id":"constructors","text":"Constructors","level":2},{"id":"constructor","text":"Constructor","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"client","text":"client","level":5},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":5},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"overrides","text":"Overrides","level":4},{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2},{"id":"options-2","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"methods","text":"Methods","level":2},{"id":"getcurrentresult","text":"getCurrentResult()","level":3},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"haslisteners","text":"hasListeners()","level":3},{"id":"returns-3","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"inherited-from","text":"Inherited from","level":4},{"id":"mutate","text":"mutate()","level":3},{"id":"parameters-2","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"variables","text":"variables","level":5},{"id":"options-3","text":"options?","level":5},{"id":"returns-4","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"example-2","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"reset","text":"reset()","level":3},{"id":"returns-5","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"see","text":"See","level":4},{"id":"example-3","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"setoptions","text":"setOptions()","level":3},{"id":"parameters-3","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"options-4","text":"options","level":5},{"id":"returns-6","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"example-4","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"subscribe","text":"subscribe()","level":3},{"id":"parameters-4","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"listener","text":"listener","level":5},{"id":"returns-7","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"example-5","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"inherited-from-2","text":"Inherited from","level":4}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:37](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L37)\n\nObserves a single mutation and derives a `MutationObserverResult` from it.\nA framework hook like `useMutation` creates one `MutationObserver` per hook\ncall, keeps it stable across re-renders, calls `setOptions` when the options\npassed to the hook change, subscribes to it to re-render on updates, and\nreads `getCurrentResult()` for the value to return. Calling `mutate()`\nbuilds a new underlying `Mutation` in the `MutationCache` and executes it.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst observer = new MutationObserver(queryClient, {\n  mutationFn: (variables: { title: string }) => addPost(variables),\n})\n```\n\n## Extends\n\n- `Subscribable`\\<`MutationObserverListener`\\<`TData`, `TError`, `TVariables`, `TOnMutateResult`\\>\\>\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` = `unknown`\n\n### TError\n\n`TError` = [`DefaultError`](../type-aliases/DefaultError.md)\n\n### TVariables\n\n`TVariables` = `void`\n\n### TOnMutateResult\n\n`TOnMutateResult` = `unknown`\n\n## Constructors\n\n### Constructor\n\n```ts\nnew MutationObserver<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>(client: QueryClient, options: MutationObserverOptions<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>): MutationObserver<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:57](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L57)\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### client\n\n[`QueryClient`](QueryClient.md)\n\n##### options\n\n[`MutationObserverOptions`](../interfaces/MutationObserverOptions.md)\\<`TData`, `TError`, `TVariables`, `TOnMutateResult`\\>\n\n#### Returns\n\n`MutationObserver`\\<`TData`, `TError`, `TVariables`, `TOnMutateResult`\\>\n\n#### Overrides\n\n```ts\nSubscribable<\n  MutationObserverListener<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>\n>.constructor\n```\n\n## Properties\n\n### options\n\n```ts\noptions: MutationObserverOptions<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:45](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L45)\n\n## Methods\n\n### getCurrentResult()\n\n```ts\ngetCurrentResult(): MutationObserverResult<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:165](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L165)\n\nReturns the observer's current result, derived from the observed\nmutation's state (or the default, `idle` state if no mutation has been\nbuilt yet, e.g. before the first `mutate()` call or after `reset()`).\n\n#### Returns\n\n[`MutationObserverResult`](../type-aliases/MutationObserverResult.md)\\<`TData`, `TError`, `TVariables`, `TOnMutateResult`\\>\n\nThe observer's latest result.\n\n***\n\n### hasListeners()\n\n```ts\nhasListeners(): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/subscribable.ts:43](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/subscribable.ts#L43)\n\nReturns `true` while at least one listener is registered, `false` once they have all unsubscribed.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n`true` if at least one listener is registered.\n\n#### Inherited from\n\n```ts\nSubscribable.hasListeners\n```\n\n***\n\n### mutate()\n\n```ts\nmutate(variables: TVariables, options?: MutateOptions<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>): Promise<TData>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:217](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L217)\n\nBuilds a new `Mutation` in the `MutationCache` using the observer's\ncurrent options, detaches this observer from any previously observed\nmutation, attaches it to the new one, and executes it with the given\nvariables.\n\nThe optional per-call `options` (`onSuccess`/`onError`/`onSettled`) are\ninvoked once the mutation settles, in addition to any callbacks defined\non the observer's own options.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### variables\n\n`TVariables`\n\nThe variables passed to the `mutationFn`.\n\n##### options?\n\n[`MutateOptions`](../interfaces/MutateOptions.md)\\<`TData`, `TError`, `TVariables`, `TOnMutateResult`\\>\n\nPer-call `onSuccess`, `onError`, and `onSettled` callbacks.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`TData`\\>\n\nA promise that resolves with the mutation's data, or rejects with its error.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nawait observer.mutate(\n  { title: 'New post' },\n  { onSuccess: (data) => console.log(data) },\n)\n```\n\n***\n\n### reset()\n\n```ts\nreset(): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:188](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L188)\n\nDetaches the observer from the mutation it is currently observing (if\nany) and resets the observed result back to its default, `idle` state.\n\nThis does not cancel an in-flight mutation; the mutation itself keeps\nrunning to completion and its own callbacks still fire, but this\nobserver stops reflecting its state and a subsequent `mutate()` call\nwill build a brand new mutation.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n#### See\n\n[MutationObserver#mutate](#mutate)\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nobserver.reset()\n```\n\n***\n\n### setOptions()\n\n```ts\nsetOptions(options: MutationObserverOptions<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:100](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L100)\n\nUpdates the observer's options.\n\nIf the new `mutationKey` differs from the previous one (and both were\ndefined), the observer is reset, detaching it from the mutation it was\nobserving. Otherwise, if the currently observed mutation is still\n`pending`, its options are updated in place as well.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### options\n\n[`MutationObserverOptions`](../interfaces/MutationObserverOptions.md)\\<`TData`, `TError`, `TVariables`, `TOnMutateResult`\\>\n\nThe new mutation observer options. They are defaulted with [QueryClient#defaultMutationOptions](QueryClient.md#defaultmutationoptions) before being applied.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nobserver.setOptions({\n  mutationFn: (variables: { title: string }) => addPost(variables),\n  onSuccess: (data) => console.log(data),\n})\n```\n\n***\n\n### subscribe()\n\n```ts\nsubscribe(listener: MutationObserverListener): () => void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/subscribable.ts:28](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/subscribable.ts#L28)\n\nRegisters a listener to be called on every update this object notifies about. Returns a function\nthat removes the listener again — call it to stop listening. The base class never drops a listener\non its own, though some subclasses clear all of theirs in `destroy()`.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### listener\n\n`MutationObserverListener`\n\nCalled on each update, with whatever the subclass passes to its subscribers.\n\n#### Returns\n\nA function that removes the listener.\n\n() => `void`\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst unsubscribe = subscribable.subscribe(() => {\n  // react to the update\n})\n\nunsubscribe()\n```\n\n#### Inherited from\n\n```ts\nSubscribable.subscribe\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: MutationObserver\ntitle: MutationObserver\n---\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:37](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L37)\n\nObserves a single mutation and derives a `MutationObserverResult` from it.\nA framework hook like `useMutation` creates one `MutationObserver` per hook\ncall, keeps it stable across re-renders, calls `setOptions` when the options\npassed to the hook change, subscribes to it to re-render on updates, and\nreads `getCurrentResult()` for the value to return. Calling `mutate()`\nbuilds a new underlying `Mutation` in the `MutationCache` and executes it.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst observer = new MutationObserver(queryClient, {\n  mutationFn: (variables: { title: string }) => addPost(variables),\n})\n```\n\n## Extends\n\n- `Subscribable`\\<`MutationObserverListener`\\<`TData`, `TError`, `TVariables`, `TOnMutateResult`\\>\\>\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` = `unknown`\n\n### TError\n\n`TError` = [`DefaultError`](../type-aliases/DefaultError.md)\n\n### TVariables\n\n`TVariables` = `void`\n\n### TOnMutateResult\n\n`TOnMutateResult` = `unknown`\n\n## Constructors\n\n### Constructor\n\n```ts\nnew MutationObserver<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>(client: QueryClient, options: MutationObserverOptions<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>): MutationObserver<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:57](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L57)\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### client\n\n[`QueryClient`](QueryClient.md)\n\n##### options\n\n[`MutationObserverOptions`](../interfaces/MutationObserverOptions.md)\\<`TData`, `TError`, `TVariables`, `TOnMutateResult`\\>\n\n#### Returns\n\n`MutationObserver`\\<`TData`, `TError`, `TVariables`, `TOnMutateResult`\\>\n\n#### Overrides\n\n```ts\nSubscribable<\n  MutationObserverListener<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>\n>.constructor\n```\n\n## Properties\n\n### options\n\n```ts\noptions: MutationObserverOptions<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:45](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L45)\n\n## Methods\n\n### getCurrentResult()\n\n```ts\ngetCurrentResult(): MutationObserverResult<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:165](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L165)\n\nReturns the observer's current result, derived from the observed\nmutation's state (or the default, `idle` state if no mutation has been\nbuilt yet, e.g. before the first `mutate()` call or after `reset()`).\n\n#### Returns\n\n[`MutationObserverResult`](../type-aliases/MutationObserverResult.md)\\<`TData`, `TError`, `TVariables`, `TOnMutateResult`\\>\n\nThe observer's latest result.\n\n***\n\n### hasListeners()\n\n```ts\nhasListeners(): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/subscribable.ts:43](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/subscribable.ts#L43)\n\nReturns `true` while at least one listener is registered, `false` once they have all unsubscribed.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n`true` if at least one listener is registered.\n\n#### Inherited from\n\n```ts\nSubscribable.hasListeners\n```\n\n***\n\n### mutate()\n\n```ts\nmutate(variables: TVariables, options?: MutateOptions<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>): Promise<TData>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:217](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L217)\n\nBuilds a new `Mutation` in the `MutationCache` using the observer's\ncurrent options, detaches this observer from any previously observed\nmutation, attaches it to the new one, and executes it with the given\nvariables.\n\nThe optional per-call `options` (`onSuccess`/`onError`/`onSettled`) are\ninvoked once the mutation settles, in addition to any callbacks defined\non the observer's own options.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### variables\n\n`TVariables`\n\nThe variables passed to the `mutationFn`.\n\n##### options?\n\n[`MutateOptions`](../interfaces/MutateOptions.md)\\<`TData`, `TError`, `TVariables`, `TOnMutateResult`\\>\n\nPer-call `onSuccess`, `onError`, and `onSettled` callbacks.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`TData`\\>\n\nA promise that resolves with the mutation's data, or rejects with its error.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nawait observer.mutate(\n  { title: 'New post' },\n  { onSuccess: (data) => console.log(data) },\n)\n```\n\n***\n\n### reset()\n\n```ts\nreset(): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:188](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L188)\n\nDetaches the observer from the mutation it is currently observing (if\nany) and resets the observed result back to its default, `idle` state.\n\nThis does not cancel an in-flight mutation; the mutation itself keeps\nrunning to completion and its own callbacks still fire, but this\nobserver stops reflecting its state and a subsequent `mutate()` call\nwill build a brand new mutation.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n#### See\n\n[MutationObserver#mutate](#mutate)\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nobserver.reset()\n```\n\n***\n\n### setOptions()\n\n```ts\nsetOptions(options: MutationObserverOptions<TData, TError, TVariables, TOnMutateResult>): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts:100](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/mutationObserver.ts#L100)\n\nUpdates the observer's options.\n\nIf the new `mutationKey` differs from the previous one (and both were\ndefined), the observer is reset, detaching it from the mutation it was\nobserving. Otherwise, if the currently observed mutation is still\n`pending`, its options are updated in place as well.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### options\n\n[`MutationObserverOptions`](../interfaces/MutationObserverOptions.md)\\<`TData`, `TError`, `TVariables`, `TOnMutateResult`\\>\n\nThe new mutation observer options. They are defaulted with [QueryClient#defaultMutationOptions](QueryClient.md#defaultmutationoptions) before being applied.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nobserver.setOptions({\n  mutationFn: (variables: { title: string }) => addPost(variables),\n  onSuccess: (data) => console.log(data),\n})\n```\n\n***\n\n### subscribe()\n\n```ts\nsubscribe(listener: MutationObserverListener): () => void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/subscribable.ts:28](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/subscribable.ts#L28)\n\nRegisters a listener to be called on every update this object notifies about. Returns a function\nthat removes the listener again — call it to stop listening. The base class never drops a listener\non its own, though some subclasses clear all of theirs in `destroy()`.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### listener\n\n`MutationObserverListener`\n\nCalled on each update, with whatever the subclass passes to its subscribers.\n\n#### Returns\n\nA function that removes the listener.\n\n() => `void`\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst unsubscribe = subscribable.subscribe(() => {\n  // react to the update\n})\n\nunsubscribe()\n```\n\n#### Inherited from\n\n```ts\nSubscribable.subscribe\n```\n"}
